eview\n\n## Versions\n\nTowards Rationale-Answer Alignment of LVLMs via Self-Rationale Calibrationicml · 2025PresentationTowards Rationale-Answer Alignment of LVLMs via Self-Rationale Calibrationarxiv · 2025 · DBLPTowards Rationale-Answer Alignment of LVLMs via Self-Rationale Calibrationarxiv · 2025 · arXiv, OpenReview\n\n## Introduction\n\nLarge Vision-Language Models (LVLMs), such as LLaVA, have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in Visual Question Answering (VQA). However, these models frequently exhibit a \"logic gap\"—a phenomenon where the model arrives at the correct answer through flawed or counterfactual reasoning. For instance, a model might correctly identify the number of objects in an image but provide a rationale that cites non-existent visual features. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n李晓强-上海大学计算机工程与科学学院 (https://cs.shu.edu.cn/info/1471/40731.htm)\nciteturn8644search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; 2015年获得上海科技进步三等奖；2023年获得上海技术发明二等奖；2017年获得获上海市级教学成果奖一等奖。 ... Yuanchen Wu, Ke Yan, Shouhong Ding,  Xiaoqiang Li,, Towards Rationale-Answer Alignment of LVLMs via Self-Rationale Calibration.\nACMM2025.2.Ziyun Dai, Xiaoqiang Li, Shaohua Zhang, Yuanchen Wu, Jide Li. See different, think better: Visual Variations Mitigating Hallucinations in LVLMs. ACMM 2025. 3.Chao yin, Stepwise Decomposition and Dual-stream Focus: A Novel Approach for Training-free Camouflaged Object Segmentation. ACMM2025.4.Yuanchen Wu, Ke Yan, Shouhong Ding,  Xiaoqiang Li,, Towards Rationale-Answer Alignment of LVLMs via Self-Rationale Calibration. ICML2025. 5.Yuhang Li, Tong Liu, Yangguang Cui, Ming Hu, Xiaoqiang Li, One Arrow, Two Hawks: Sharpness-aware Minimization for Federated Learning via Global Model Trajectory, ICML2025.  6.Yuanchen Wu, Lu Zhang, Hang Yao, Junlong Du, Ke Yan, Shouhong Ding, Yunsheng Wu, Xiaoqiang Li. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYua